<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>From Paper to Pipeline — Madeleine Smith</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Crimson+Pro:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #EDE4F3;          /* lavender — matches homepage page bg */
    --surface: #FAF7F2;     /* cream — for cream text on dark cards */
    --bg-soft: #E8E0D4;     /* parchment — warm neutral surface */
    --bg-card: #D5CAE0;     /* lavender divider tone */
    --ink: #3D2E52;         /* dark plum — matches homepage --text */
    --ink-soft: #6B5A80;    /* muted plum — matches homepage --text-muted */
    --ink-faint: #6B5A80;   /* same as ink-soft for readability on lavender */
    --teal: #4A7C8A;        /* pacific teal — matches homepage --accent-pacific */
    --teal-deep: #3D6373;
    --rust: #9E6B5A;        /* terracotta — matches homepage --accent-terracotta */
    --plum: #574A66;        /* deep plum — fits lavender family */
    --plum-deep: #4A3D5C;
    --rule: #E0D5C9;        /* matches homepage --border */
    --rule-faint: #D5CAE0;  /* matches homepage --divider */
    --slate: #5C6B73;       /* matches homepage --body */

    --serif: 'Crimson Pro', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
    --sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;

    --content-max: 680px;
    --shell-max: 1100px;    /* matches homepage container */
  }

  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }

  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-feature-settings: "ss01", "kern";
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;
  }

  ::selection { background: var(--rust); color: var(--surface); }

  /* ----------- LAYOUT ----------- */
  .shell {
    max-width: var(--shell-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 56px 48px 60px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 64px;
  }

  header.top {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--teal);
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 7px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--teal);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: transparent;
    transition: color 220ms ease, background 220ms ease, border-color 220ms ease;
  }
  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--bg);
    background: var(--teal);
    border-color: var(--teal);
  }

  /* ----------- SIDEBAR NAV ----------- */
  .sidenav {
    position: sticky;
    top: 56px;
    align-self: start;
    padding-top: 8px;
  }

  .sidenav ol {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .sidenav li {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .sidenav a {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--slate);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 240ms ease;
    padding: 4px 0;
  }

  .sidenav a::before {
    content: '';
    width: 18px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--slate);
    transition: width 240ms ease, background 240ms ease;
  }

  .sidenav a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  .sidenav a:hover::before { background: var(--ink); }

  .sidenav a.active {
    color: var(--rust);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .sidenav a.active::before {
    width: 28px;
    height: 1.5px;
    background: var(--rust);
  }

  /* ----------- ARTICLE ----------- */
  article {
    max-width: var(--content-max);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rust);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 420;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 144, "SOFT" 30;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5.5vw, 64px);
    line-height: 1.04;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    color: var(--teal);
    margin: 0 0 32px;
  }

  .subtitle {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 40px;
    max-width: 580px;
  }

  .byline {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 48px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 15px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rust);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 44px 0 32px;
  }

  h3 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 460;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 60, "SOFT" 30;
    font-size: 28px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--teal);
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  p em, .pullquote {
    font-style: italic;
  }

  a.inline {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    transition: border-color 220ms ease;
  }
  a.inline:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--rust); }

  /* ----------- STAT GRID ----------- */
  .stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    margin: 48px 0 56px;
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  .stat {
    background: var(--plum);
    color: var(--surface);
    padding: 36px 32px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    min-height: 180px;
  }

  .stat.tall {
    grid-row: span 2;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .stat.tall .stat-figure {
    font-size: clamp(96px, 13vw, 160px);
  }
  .stat.small { min-height: 0; padding: 24px 28px; }

  .stat-figure {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 144, "SOFT" 50;
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: clamp(48px, 6vw, 72px);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .stat.small .stat-figure {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4vw, 48px);
  }

  .stat-label {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    opacity: 0.88;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  /* ----------- NODE EXPLORER ----------- */
  .tier-intro {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .tier-explorer {
    margin: 16px 0 56px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .tier-card {
    color: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
    position: relative;
  }

  .tier-1 { background: var(--rust); }
  .tier-2 { background: var(--teal); }
  .tier-3 { background: var(--plum); }

  .tier-head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 28px;
    padding: 26px 32px;
    cursor: pointer;
    user-select: none;
    border: none;
    background: transparent;
    width: 100%;
    text-align: left;
    font-family: inherit;
    color: inherit;
  }

  .tier-num {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--surface);
    opacity: 0.65;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .tier-name {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 460;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 36, "SOFT" 30;
    font-size: 24px;
    color: var(--surface);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .tier-name .descriptor {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--surface);
    opacity: 0.78;
    margin-top: 4px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  .tier-toggle {
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1px solid rgba(250, 247, 242, 0.4);
    background: transparent;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    transition: transform 320ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1), border-color 240ms ease;
    color: var(--surface);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .tier-card.open .tier-toggle {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    border-color: var(--surface);
  }

  .tier-toggle svg { width: 12px; height: 12px; }

  .tier-body {
    max-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: max-height 480ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
  }

  .tier-card.open .tier-body {
    max-height: 800px;
  }

  .tier-body-inner {
    padding: 4px 40px 36px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 32px 40px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(250, 247, 242, 0.18);
    padding-top: 28px;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .tier-field {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .tier-field.full {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .tier-field-label {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--surface);
    opacity: 0.7;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .tier-field-body {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--surface);
  }

  /* Connector between architecture nodes — implies downward data flow */
  .node-connector {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    opacity: 0.45;
    margin: -2px 0;
  }
  .node-connector svg {
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
  }

  /* ----------- RETENTION CALLOUT ----------- */
  .retention {
    margin: 24px 0 48px;
    padding: 56px 48px;
    background: var(--teal);
    color: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 14px;
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  .retention-figure {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 144, "SOFT" 50;
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: clamp(72px, 10vw, 108px);
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .retention-figure sup {
    font-size: 0.5em;
    vertical-align: super;
    margin-left: 4px;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .retention-label {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    opacity: 0.92;
    max-width: 420px;
  }

  /* ----------- MAPPING TABLE ----------- */
  .mapping {
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 32px 36px;
    margin: 32px 0 48px;
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .mapping-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
    padding-bottom: 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .mapping-header span {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .mapping-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
    padding: 18px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .mapping-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .mapping-row .from {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .mapping-row .to {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 420;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  /* ----------- CLOSING ----------- */
  .closing {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 56px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .closing p {
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .closing .first-letter {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 144, "SOFT" 50;
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: 56px;
    line-height: 0.9;
    color: var(--rust);
    float: left;
    margin: 6px 10px -4px 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  /* ----------- FOOTER ----------- */
  footer {
    grid-column: 2 / -1;
    margin-top: 60px;
    padding-top: 40px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    max-width: var(--content-max);
  }

  footer p {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  /* ----------- MOBILE ----------- */
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .shell {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0;
      padding: 32px 24px 40px;
    }
    .sidenav { display: none; }
    header.top { margin-bottom: 28px; }
    .byline { margin-bottom: 32px; }
    h2 { margin: 32px 0 24px; }

    .stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .stat.tall { grid-row: auto; }

    .tier-head {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
      gap: 16px;
      padding: 22px 24px;
    }
    .tier-num { display: none; }
    .tier-body-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
      padding: 28px 28px 32px;
    }

    .retention { padding: 40px 28px; }
    .mapping-row, .mapping-header { gap: 16px; }

    footer {
      grid-column: 1;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 12px;
    }
  }

  /* ----------- ENTRANCE ANIMATION ----------- */
  .fade-in {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(8px);
    animation: fadeIn 800ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.6, 0.2, 1) forwards;
  }
  .fade-in:nth-child(1) { animation-delay: 0ms; }
  .fade-in:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 80ms; }
  .fade-in:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 160ms; }
  .fade-in:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: 240ms; }

  @keyframes fadeIn {
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="shell">

  <header class="top">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to home</a>
  </header>

  <nav class="sidenav" aria-label="Section navigation">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#build" data-target="build">The Build</a></li>
      <li><a href="#architecture" data-target="architecture">The Architecture</a></li>
      <li><a href="#held" data-target="held">What Held</a></li>
      <li><a href="#mapping" data-target="mapping">Where It Maps</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <main>
    <article>

      <div class="fade-in">
        <div class="eyebrow">Case Study · Evaluation Infrastructure</div>
      </div>

      <h1 class="fade-in">From Paper to Pipeline</h1>

      <p class="subtitle fade-in">Architecting a FERPA-compliant SaaS pipeline for a 150-person youth-serving nonprofit with no centralized data infrastructure.</p>

      <p class="byline fade-in">Madeleine Smith &nbsp;·&nbsp; 2025–2026</p>

      <!-- BUILD -->
      <section id="build">
        <h2>The Build</h2>

        <p>For my first year as the founding evaluation director, I sat inside a 150-person youth-serving nonprofit with no centralized data infrastructure. Program records lived in spreadsheets, intake forms ran on paper, and revenue was reconciled by hand. There was no single source of truth — not for participants, not for outcomes, not for revenue. The pilot below is how we built one.</p>

        <p>The work had federal stakes. Participant data was FERPA-protected — intake forms collected demographics, medical information, and parental consent for students enrolled across in-school program sites. Compliance had to live at the point of capture, not be retrofitted. The pipeline had to be FERPA-clean from the first record.</p>

        <p>I was a department of one, building cross-functionally with IT, Operations, and executive leadership across siloed program departments. The pilot was scoped to a single department running programs across 7 school sites — 20 staff total — with planned expansion across the org once the architecture proved out.</p>

        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat tall">
            <div class="stat-figure">600+</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Student intake records flowing through the integrated pipeline by the end of my tenure.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat small">
            <div class="stat-figure">20</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Summer programs enrolled across two departments via the system.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat small">
            <div class="stat-figure">7</div>
            <div class="stat-label">School sites onboarded in the pilot cohort.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ARCHITECTURE -->
      <section id="architecture">
        <h2>The Architecture</h2>

        <h3>A three-system SaaS pipeline, built end-to-end</h3>

        <p class="tier-intro">The pipeline was three SaaS tools connected by API into a single data flow — intake to record to revenue. Each system did one job. The integration carried the work between them so staff didn't have to.</p>

        <p class="tier-intro">FERPA compliance shaped every layer. Data collection had to be permissioned at capture, transmitted securely, and stored with role-based access. The architecture below is what that looked like in practice.</p>

        <div class="tier-explorer">

          <!-- NODE 1: FormAssembly -->
          <article class="tier-card tier-1" data-tier="1">
            <button class="tier-head" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="tier-1-body">
              <span class="tier-num">Node 01</span>
              <span class="tier-name">FormAssembly
                <span class="descriptor">Intake layer</span>
              </span>
              <span class="tier-toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                  <path d="M6 1V11M1 6H11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                </svg>
              </span>
            </button>
            <div class="tier-body" id="tier-1-body">
              <div class="tier-body-inner">
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">What it did</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">Front-door data capture. Every participant intake form lived here — demographics, medical information, parental consent forms — built to FERPA standards from the first field.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">What lived here</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">Participant demographic and medical data, parental consent records, program-specific intake fields per school site.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">Integration</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">Connected to Salesforce via API. Submitted forms wrote records directly into the central database with no manual re-entry.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">Why it mattered</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">FERPA compliance had to live at the point of capture, not be retrofitted. Building the intake layer to spec meant the rest of the pipeline inherited compliance by default.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <div class="node-connector" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <path d="M9 3 L9 15 M4 10 L9 15 L14 10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <!-- NODE 2: Salesforce -->
          <article class="tier-card tier-2" data-tier="2">
            <button class="tier-head" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="tier-2-body">
              <span class="tier-num">Node 02</span>
              <span class="tier-name">Salesforce
                <span class="descriptor">Record layer</span>
              </span>
              <span class="tier-toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                  <path d="M6 1V11M1 6H11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                </svg>
              </span>
            </button>
            <div class="tier-body" id="tier-2-body">
              <div class="tier-body-inner">
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">What it did</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">The central record store and workflow hub. Every participant record lived here. Program staff worked here daily — enrollment, attendance, outcomes.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">What lived here</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">All participant records, program enrollment data, outcome tracking, staff activity logs, role-based permissions.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">Integration</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">Received records from FormAssembly via API; passed payment data to Stripe; served as the single source of truth across the pipeline.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">Why it mattered</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">Replaced disconnected spreadsheets with one database that staff actually worked in. The system stopped being a reporting requirement and started being a daily tool.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <div class="node-connector" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
              <path d="M9 3 L9 15 M4 10 L9 15 L14 10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <!-- NODE 3: Stripe -->
          <article class="tier-card tier-3" data-tier="3">
            <button class="tier-head" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="tier-3-body">
              <span class="tier-num">Node 03</span>
              <span class="tier-name">Stripe
                <span class="descriptor">Revenue layer</span>
              </span>
              <span class="tier-toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
